<title>MEXICO: Six top Mexican business leaders to visit Britain.</title>
<headline>Six top Mexican business leaders to visit Britain.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six high-level Mexican business leaders will visit Britain next week at the invitation of the British government to promote trade, the British embassy said on Thursday in a news release.</p>
<p>The group will meet with Prime Minister John Major and other top government officials as part of an agreement to promote bilateral trade signed between Major and Mexican President Ernesto Zedillo during Zedillo's visit to London in January, the embassy said.</p>
<p>The Mexicans scheduled to make the trip are Dionisio Garza Medina, president and CEO of Grupo Alfa; Tomas Gonzalez Sada, president and CEO of Grupo Cydsa; Roberto Hernandez Ramirez, chairman of the board of Banamex; Bernardo Quintana, president of Grupo ICA; Claudio X. Gonzalez, president and CEO of Kimberly Clark de Mexico; and Carlos Slim Helu, president of Grupo Carso.</p>
<p>--Dan Trotta, Mexico City newsroom, (525) 728-9507</p>
